            "id": 1520,
            "sort": 1,
            "name": "Introduction",
            "value": "<p>While some museums offer free admission, many charge for it. Although charging admission fees may create certain barriers, I believe the advantages of this practice significantly outweigh the disadvantages.</p>",
            "question_id": 17816,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 1521,
            "sort": 2,
            "name": "Body 1",
            "value": "<p><strong>Admittedly, museum admission fees can pose some challenges for specific groups of people.</strong> <span style=\"color: rgb(22, 145, 121);\">One major concern is reduced educational access for students who often have limited budgets. Many students cannot afford museum visits, causing them to miss out on valuable learning experiences such as history or science lessons, which ultimately increases educational inequality.</span> <span style=\"color: rgb(35, 111, 161);\">Additionally, high admission fees can have a negative tourism impact in certain areas. When fees deter tourists, fewer visitors come to the city or region, leading local businesses like hotels and restaurants to lose revenue and creating a negative economic impact on the local community.</span></p>",
            "question_id": 17816,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 1522,
            "sort": 3,
            "name": "Body 2",
            "value": "<p><strong>However, I believe these drawbacks are outweighed by the significant benefits of charging admission. </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(22, 145, 121);\">Most importantly, admission fees provide steady revenue for museums to afford proper maintenance of artifacts and preserve cultural heritage for future generations. This ensures that exhibits remain in good condition and can be enjoyed by visitors for years to come.</span><span style=\"color: rgb(35, 111, 161);\"> Furthermore, the extra revenue from tickets allows museums to invest in educational programs and research projects. They can hire qualified educators and researchers, ultimately providing better learning experiences for visitors and contributing to knowledge advancement.</span></p>",
            "question_id": 17816,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 1523,
            "sort": 4,
            "name": "Conclusion",
            "value": "<p>In conclusion, while charging museum admission may create some barriers for students and affect local tourism, the benefits in terms of heritage preservation and educational investment are more substantial.</p>",
            "question_id": 17816,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          }
